{
  "opportunity_id": "proc_83841e6f14",
  "source": "content_cluster",
  "title": "Correcting stale deal prices in Sitara, then redrafting in Unify",
  "task_class": "deal_entry_correction",
  "label_mechanical": "Deal entry and correction in Sitara / Unify / TAGG: correct price / deal / sitara",
  "narrative": {
    "what_happens": "Someone reconciling an invoice or a trader's book finds that the price recorded against a deal in Sitara does not match the price actually billed or agreed. They email the person who can edit the deal, quoting the deal number, the flow date and both prices, and ask for the record to be updated. The editor changes the price in Sitara and replies to confirm; where an invoice or draft already exists downstream, they tell the requester to redraft in Unify so the two systems agree. In some instances the price has to be checked against a trader's own book or spreadsheet before anyone can say which figure is right, and in at least one thread a first correction was itself wrong and had to be revised again by hour block.",
    "where_it_stalls": "Every message in this cluster carries a rework signal: the deal was already entered, and the work is redoing it. The stall is that Sitara is not updated when a price changes, so the error only surfaces later at invoicing, and the requester cannot fix it themselves \u2014 they must hand the deal number to whoever holds edit rights, and then wait for a confirmation before redrafting in Unify. Because Sitara and Unify do not agree automatically, one correction becomes two manual steps in two systems, and the authoritative price sometimes lives in a trader's book or spreadsheet rather than either system.",
    "why_it_recurs": "Prices are re-set each month for the same deals, and nothing forces Sitara to be updated when they change; the mismatch is caught only when invoicing or reconciliation compares systems, which happens every cycle.",
    "automation_opportunity": "A scheduled comparison of each active Sitara deal price against the invoiced or booked price, flagging mismatches by deal number and flow month before invoicing, and propagating any Sitara price edit into Unify so the redraft request stops travelling by email.",
    "coherence": "tight"
  },
